# Global excludes. `.claude/worktrees/` is where Claude Code puts the worktrees
# it creates, and — through ~/.config/worktrunk/config.toml — where `wt` puts
# its too. A nested worktree is a `.git` file plus a full checkout, so without
# this every repo shows an untracked `.claude/` the moment either tool is used.
.claude/worktrees/
